<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tambov Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tambov Rebellion was a peasant uprising against Bolshevik rule in Tambov province, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, in 1920–1921. Led by Alexander Antonov and provoked by forced grain requisitioning, it grew to tens of thousands of fighters. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-tukhachevsky">Mikhail Tukhachevsky</a> suppressed it with mass hostage-taking, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportations</a> and the use of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poison-gas">poison gas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tambov-rebellion.jpg" alt="Tambov Rebellion" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: P. S. Burton after Memnon335bc · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tambov_Rebellion.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The result was economic collapse, peasant revolts such as that in <b>Tambov</b>, and the famine of 1921–1922, which killed several million people.</blockquote><a href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
